# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Range-distribution reshard (tablet split / merge).
#
# These exist because a forced split finishes in well under a second, so no external fault
# (an FE restart takes ~17s) can land inside RUNNING. Arm one WITH PAUSE to freeze the job at
# that phase, act externally, then ADMIN DISABLE FAILPOINT to release.
#
# Where a pause parks -- read this before arming one:
#   * All six rules below park the SINGLE TabletReshardJobMgr daemon thread, which runs
#     ColocateChecker.runOneCycle(), drainReshardCandidates() and runTabletReshardJobs() in
#     sequence. So any one of them freezes every reshard job AND colocate convergence on that
#     frontend, and only one can be in effect at a time. The daemon loop has no watchdog, so a
#     park just means missed ticks.
#   * NEVER write a rule inside SplitTabletJob/MergeTabletJob.addNewMaterializedIndexes: it holds
#     the table WRITE lock, so parking there makes the table unavailable to queries and DDL for
#     the whole pause. The two *_before_metadata_switch rules below deliberately sit at the CALL
#     to it, which is outside every lock.
#
# Every DO is a safe no-op, so arming one of these with ENABLE instead of PAUSE skips one daemon
# tick rather than corrupting a job.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Generic amplifier: hold any reshard job at its current state so an external fault (kill a CN,
# switch the leader, partition the network) lands while the job is still in flight. Note run()
# catches Exception and aborts the job, so DO throw here would inject a job FAILURE, not a pause.
RULE tablet_reshard_job_run
CLASS com.starrocks.alter.reshard.TabletReshardJob
METHOD run()
HELPER com.starrocks.failpoint.FailPointHelper
IF shouldTrigger("tablet_reshard_job_run")
DO return;
ENDRULE

# Split points computed and the split transaction published, catalog NOT yet switched. Kill the
# leader here and the follower must take over with the tablet set and ranges exactly as before.
RULE split_before_metadata_switch
CLASS com.starrocks.alter.reshard.SplitTabletJob
METHOD runRunningJob
AT INVOKE addNewMaterializedIndexes
HELPER com.starrocks.failpoint.FailPointHelper
IF shouldTrigger("split_before_metadata_switch")
DO return;
ENDRULE

# Merge peer of split_before_metadata_switch.
RULE merge_before_metadata_switch
CLASS com.starrocks.alter.reshard.MergeTabletJob
METHOD runRunningJob
AT INVOKE addNewMaterializedIndexes
HELPER com.starrocks.failpoint.FailPointHelper
IF shouldTrigger("merge_before_metadata_switch")
DO return;
ENDRULE

# Catalog switched and the CLEANING transition already journalled (setJobState writes
# logUpdateTabletReshardJob), job not yet FINISHED. Restart here and replay must be idempotent:
# ranges contiguous, no overlap, no duplicate tablet id.
RULE split_after_metadata_switch
CLASS com.starrocks.alter.reshard.SplitTabletJob
METHOD runCleaningJob
AT ENTRY
HELPER com.starrocks.failpoint.FailPointHelper
IF shouldTrigger("split_after_metadata_switch")
DO return;
ENDRULE

# Merge peer of split_after_metadata_switch.
RULE merge_after_metadata_switch
CLASS com.starrocks.alter.reshard.MergeTabletJob
METHOD runCleaningJob
AT ENTRY
HELPER com.starrocks.failpoint.FailPointHelper
IF shouldTrigger("merge_after_metadata_switch")
DO return;
ENDRULE

# Colocate cross-table alignment, per table. AT EXIT, not AT ENTRY: the trigger has no table
# predicate or call counter, so an armed PAUSE stops the FIRST invocation of the cycle. At ENTRY that
# would mean no table was processed at all -- a not-started group, not a mid-alignment one. At EXIT the
# first table of the group has been processed (its alignment job fired, if it needed one) and the next
# has not, which is the partially-processed state "fail-close or full rollback" must be asserted
# against. Note the fired job cannot run while this rule is parked: it would run on this same daemon
# thread. false is what the method already returns for "work still needed, retry next cycle".
RULE colocate_mid_align_table
CLASS com.starrocks.alter.reshard.ColocateChecker
METHOD alignTableIfApplicable
AT EXIT
HELPER com.starrocks.failpoint.FailPointHelper
IF shouldTrigger("colocate_mid_align_table")
DO return false;
ENDRULE
